 one patch-agent session complete more than one reviewed patch without a later hash replacing earlier
 reviewed work in the linearizer prompt.
 
+When a review completes with no findings, the controller appends a feature-completion confirmation
+to the reviewed patch-agent session and selects that session. A `yes` or `y` reply records the
+feature as done without sending a prompt to the agent backend; a `no` or `n` reply leaves the session
+open. Later non-confirmation chat to a done feature reopens the patch-agent session and sends the
+message through the normal agent-send path.
+
 The command transcript is also the conversation history for the persistent `command-agent`. That
 system agent interprets chat sent to the Work Leaf command surface. It recognizes literal command
 lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching
@@ -293,6 +299,11 @@ state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transi
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
 again.
 
+Feature-completion confirmations use the same controller session lines in terminal mode. A confirmed
+done patch-agent chat is hidden from the left pane and the command interface becomes selected. When
+the user types later chat while that done feature is the most recently closed session, the terminal
+adapter restores the session, selects it, and routes the chat back through `WorkLeafController`.
+
 `src/ui.rs::TerminalUi` owns terminal-specific presentation state:
 
 - `UiMode`, `PaneFocus`, `UiSurface`, `UiKey`, and `UiAction` model terminal interactions.
